%N A398264 Numbers divisible by the square but not the cube of their least prime factor.
%C A398264 From _Amiram Eldar_, Jul 26 2026: (Start)
%C A398264 The asymptotic density of terms with least prime factor prime(n) (within all the positive integers) is d(n) = (1/prime(n)^2 - 1/prime(n)^3) * Product_{k=1..(n-1)} (1-1/prime(k)). For example, for n = 1, 2, 3, 4, 5 and 6, d(n) = 1/8, 1/27, 4/375, 8/1715, 16/9317 and 192/169169.
%C A398264 The asymptotic density of this sequence is Sum_{n>=1} d(n) = 0.1827640768693... . (End)
%H A398264 Michael De Vlieger, <a href="/A398264/b398264.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10000</a>
%t A398264 Select[Range[325], FactorInteger[#][[1, -1]] == 2 &] (* _Michael De Vlieger_, Jul 24 2026 *)
%o A398264 (PARI) isok(n) = n > 1 && factor(n)[1, 2] == 2;
